            <ArticleTitle>Management of a patient admitted with acute non-ST-elevation MI.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>293-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case study reviews the history, symptoms, management and rehabilitation of a patient admitted to accident and emergency with severe chest pain. After other conditions had been ruled out he was diagnosed with acute non-ST-elevation myocardial infarction. He later underwent a coronary angioplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
